--- a/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5
+++ b/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5
@@ -4076,6 +4076,21 @@
 .IP
 
 .TP
+\fBbf_max_job_array_launch\fR=\#
+The maximum number of outstanding preemption launch transactions per job array.
+Each prepared task is split into its own pending job record before its node
+plan is committed or victims are signaled. Preparation slots count against
+the array's concurrency limit in addition to running tasks. A committed owner
+can use its reserved slot; other tasks cannot consume it. Slots are released
+on start, cancellation, transaction teardown, or completed failure cleanup.
+This limit is independent of \fBbf_max_job_array_resv\fR. Zero prevents new
+array preemption transactions, but does not prevent idle-resource starts,
+ordinary non-array preemption, or retries of existing plans. Lowering the limit
+does not discard existing plans. Victim QOS GraceTime is unchanged.
+Default: 20, Min: 0, Max: 1000.
+.IP
+
+.TP
 \fBbf_max_job_array_resv\fR=\#
 The maximum number of tasks from a job array for which the backfill scheduler
 will reserve resources in the future.
